# String#% with an Array (not a Tuple literal) is rejected by the checker.
# Sake: error: Arithmetic.%: the operands are (String, String[]@L5), which the left operand's type does not support
# Ruby: prints "a-b". (The cheat sheet shows `"%d-%s" % [a, b]`, a Tuple, which works.)
# Hit in SafeBuffer#% (core_ext/string/safe_buffer.sake), written as `format(@str, *xs)` instead.
xs = String["a", "b"]
p("%s-%s" % xs)
